Z||000003||Robert||04-11-2000||11:21 PM||||One on my 4 sisters is a Deputy Sheriff.  When she was a teenager she volunteered at our local police department.  Then she went to the local junior college that had a course in law enforcement.  She enjoys her job, but wants to get into transportation of prisoners some day.   On the money side, she makes over $60,000.  Not bad for two years of college.  Of course she does have to deal with the seedier side of society.  One thing nice about having a Sheriff in the family, besides having her business card in my wallet for those unforeseen times when I get stopped by the law, is I almost always get dismissed from jury duty||||reg||10
Z||000004||Boodoggin||04-11-2000||11:29 PM||||Wow! 60k a year thats awesomee.  Transportation of prisoners is a high paying job also, it's one of those risky jobs few want to do, so they get paid a lot, like x-ray technicians start out at $40-50 per hour because x-rays can be harmfull. ||||reg||10
Z||000005||BN Boomer||04-12-2000||12:51 AM||||After wrecking my Fiero a few weeks back, a got to spend a bit of quality time with a Wahington State Patrolman while waiting for the tow truck to show. Turns out he had just recently graduated from the WSP academy. Said he'd been a grocer for the previous 9 years! Anyhow, he said the WSP is actually have a tough time recruiting qualified applicants and many positions were going unfilled. Might keep them in mind.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>The thought of becoming a State Patrolman briefly crossed my mind, but then I'm already making 50K a year, work less than 35 hours per week, and haven't yet been shot at.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000006||sully5||04-12-2000||08:19 AM||||Good luck to ya. I'm not in law enforcement, but I'm a firefighter so I know a lot of police officers. Went to Eastern Kentucky Univ. and got a degree in fire and safety. It is part of the College ofLaw Enforcement. I think our local police start at around $30K, but I am not sure. Good luck to ya.||||reg||1
Z||000007||stsmithgt||04-13-2000||09:40 AM||||I've support the need of several law enforcment officers through the years.  I've donated thousands of dollars towards those career types. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  My dad was even a deputy sheriff way back when.  I've hopefully retired those habits of mine though it's tough driving legal (slow) in a Fiero, but good luck in finding others who want to contribute to the demand for more law enforcers. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000008||turbo86se||04-13-2000||11:48 AM||||Boodoggin, looks like we're in the same boat! This has been my first year back in school at Horry Tech, and I'm taking the Criminal Justice classes seeking my Associates. I love the classes, everything is fascinating!!  BTW, just got a 90 on my Constitutional Law test! Should have been a 100, but I messed up on the curtliage part of the test! <BR>Hopefully I'll get my Associates in 2 years, but I'm not sure what I'm going to take on as a career. Accident investigation and forensics to me are fascinating, so we'll see!!<BR>Good luck to ya!!!       -joel||||reg||1
